  "description": "DETTUV crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group I 2 2 2. Reported CIF formula moiety: C36 H74 Gd9 N8 O58 1+,H1 O1 1-,2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd1B (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd2B (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd1C (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd2C (Gd) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.578-5.123 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.99-167.26°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula {Gd9(L)4(μ4-OH)2(μ3-OH)8(μ2-OCH3)4(NO3)8(H2O)8}(OH)·2H2O (HL = 2,6-dimethoxyphenol). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
